Sections "PROJECT" contain missmatched items: {'PROJECT_SUMMARY': ["The microbiome plays an established, complex role in role in the development of neurodegenerative diseases. However, the individual microbes that influence degeneration, and the molecular mechanisms by which these microbes positively or negatively affect the degenerating nervous system is an area of active investigation. Utilizing a C. elegans model of chronic axon degeneration we screened bacterial diets and identified Comamonas aquatica (C. aquatica) as significantly protective against TIR-1/SARM1 induced axon degeneration. Through both genetic and metabolic analyses we find that a C. aquatica diet provides the metabolite B12, which lowers toxic homocysteine levels through METR-1/MTR methionine synthase activity in the intestine. Additionally, B12 supplementation alone is sufficient to protect against axon degeneration and lower homocysteine levels. This work contributes significantly to our understanding of the gut-brain axis and how gut bacteria can alter the host's metabolic state and protect the degenerating nervous system.", "The microbiome plays an established, complex role in role in the development of neurodegenerative diseases. However, the individual microbes that influence degeneration, and the molecular mechanisms by which these microbes positively or negatively affect the degenerating nervous system is an area of active investigation. Utilizing a C. elegans model of chronic axon degeneration we screened bacterial diets and identified Comamonas aquatica (C. aquatica) as significantly protective against TIR-1/SARM1 induced axon degeneration. Through both genetic and metabolic analyses we find that a C. aquatica diet provides the metabolite B12, which lowers toxic homocysteine levels through METR-1/MTR methionine synthase activity in the intestine. Additionally, B12 supplementation alone is sufficient to protect against axon degeneration and lower homocysteine levels. This work contribut